Z||000000||firstfiero||04-29-2001||05:20 PM||||     Don't know if any of you watch this show on TNN but this week they were at an all pontiac show and not only did they mention fieros being part of the show but they showed one. Who knows maybe next time they'll talk to the owner and give them some recignition. Another cool part of the show was when they went to a classic restore shop. They did everything in house. They rip out every bolt and  piece of wire...generally everything that could be removed from the frame and replace it or restore it. Takes 1 and a half to 2 years!! They even take pictures and mail them to you to show every step of the restore. They didn't say how much but I'm sure it was a pretty penny to have work done like that!  ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Phil||04-29-2001||06:06 PM||||Some of those "full" restorations start at $75000.00||||reg||1
